{"id": 29, "ts": 1781599941.6063144, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "agent_2", "message": "I\u2019m less convinced that Candidate\u202fD is our best choice. While D certainly takes responsibility seriously, concentrates well, and solves problems effectively, the new input from Anna shows his stress\u2011resilience is only \u201cadequate\u201d \u2013 he \u201cresponds to unexpected events adequately.\u201d That is a far weaker indicator than Candidate\u202fB\u2019s proven ability to \u201chandle stress very well.\u201d Moreover, we still have no evidence of D\u2019s crew\u2011cooperation, and his known hot temper and know\u2011it\u2011all attitude raise serious doubts about how he will interact with a cockpit crew on long\u2011haul flights. In contrast, Candidate\u202fB is very conscientious, handles stress well, and demonstrates solid technical judgment (weather assessment, computer skills). Although B makes occasional nasty remarks, those are less likely to impair safety than a hot temper that could flare under pressure. Given the stronger stress\u2011resilience and clearer evidence of reliability for B, I now recommend Candidate\u202fB as the preferred hire."}
